{
  "description": "Hand-derived golden set for the deterministic report-audit helpers (phase 6, feature 10). Every expectation was derived by hand from the documented parsing rules (ASCII + Devanagari digits, comma/dot grouping, day-first slash dates, span reproduction, verbatim quote checks) and cross-checked against the pure engine. No model, database, network or storage is involved.",
  "limitations": [
    "fixtures are synthetic; real-world amount/date/claim variety is broader than this set",
    "the model's claim extraction and support assessment are out of scope for the golden set - only their parse accept/reject and quote-verification contracts are checked here",
    "cross-claim currency conflicts use the documented digit-key heuristic; two legitimately different amounts may surface for reviewer judgment",
    "counter-evidence token extraction is checked deterministically; the record scan itself runs against real source records in the API and live sections"
  ],
